; The ONE variable: `z_index` on the Node2D a Control was PROMOTED past.
; `p_z = CLAMP(p_z + ci->z_index, ...)` accumulates through every item the
; cull walk descends (renderer_canvas_cull.cpp:430-434), and a skipped Node2D
; is one of them — so the red bar, authored FIRST, draws over the blue one
; that follows it. The other promoted-ancestor fixtures move the transform,
; the tint and the visibility, each of which reaches the Control through a
; different carrier, and all of them leave `z_index` at 0.
; Without the ancestor's z, file order alone decides and the blue bar wins the
; overlap.

